00:54:47.920 --> 00:54:54.560
&gt;&gt; The Master of Arts in Business
Research,

00:54:54.560 --> 00:54:59.290
recognizes the accomplishments of students
who have completed the course work, and

00:54:59.290 --> 00:55:02.890
fulfilled the research requirements of the
Masters degree.

00:55:02.890 --> 00:55:05.970
And thus, have become domain experts.

00:55:05.970 --> 00:55:11.340
But are not continuing on to do the
further work required for the PhD degree.

00:55:11.340 --> 00:55:15.855
This year's candidate for Master of Arts
in Business Research is Aaron Lee.

00:55:15.855 --> 00:55:21.310
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:55:21.310 --> 00:55:24.070
&gt;&gt; So this year marks the 42nd class of
students who

00:55:24.070 --> 00:55:27.740
graduate with a certificate in public
management and social innovation.

00:55:29.040 --> 00:55:32.990
Founded by Dean Emeritus RJ Miller, the
certificate program educates leaders

00:55:32.990 --> 00:55:35.910
committed to social and environmental
change.

00:55:35.910 --> 00:55:40.860
Today's graduates earning the certificate
really do embody the spirit of our motto,

00:55:40.860 --> 00:55:45.140
Change lives, change organizations, change
the world.

00:55:45.140 --> 00:55:48.230
These students have already shown their
commitment using management skills to

00:55:48.230 --> 00:55:50.620
alleviate global social problems.

00:55:50.620 --> 00:55:55.100
For example, they participated in a wide
range of social innovation courses

00:55:55.100 --> 00:56:00.330
covering topics such as social enterprise,
health care innovation, the business of

00:56:00.330 --> 00:56:05.450
education, business at the bottom of the
pyramid, and sustainable energy markets.

00:56:06.580 --> 00:56:10.030
They explored roles with high social
impact such as board governance,

00:56:10.030 --> 00:56:11.830
impact investing, and philanthropy.

00:56:13.460 --> 00:56:18.572
They traveled on social innovation study
trips to places like, Argentina, Brazil,

00:56:18.572 --> 00:56:25.310
Cambodia, Vietnam, India, Kenya, and Nepal
among others.

00:56:25.310 --> 00:56:29.290
To see for themselves what is being done
to address extreme poverty,

00:56:29.290 --> 00:56:31.450
urban migrations, sustainability, and
more.

00:56:32.670 --> 00:56:35.300
Some of these students have developed
their own social enterprise and

00:56:35.300 --> 00:56:37.040
are ready to launch right after
graduation.

00:56:37.040 --> 00:56:40.620
I am proud to tell you that this year, we

00:56:40.620 --> 00:56:45.640
have 99 recipients of the certificate in
Public Management and Social Innovation.

00:56:45.640 --> 00:56:48.800
Their names are listed in the commencement
program.

00:56:48.800 --> 00:56:52.445
I now ask those 99 students to stand.

00:56:52.445 --> 00:56:55.680
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE].

00:56:55.680 --> 00:56:57.380
&gt;&gt; And I would like us to recognize him
for

00:56:57.380 --> 00:57:02.090
completing a formal course of study in the
Management of Public Nonproft and

00:57:02.090 --> 00:57:06.290
Social Issue Organizations in addition to
earning our MBA and MSX degrees.

00:57:07.480 --> 00:57:08.194
Congratulations.

00:57:08.194 --> 00:57:16.590
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE].

00:57:16.590 --> 00:57:18.650
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon on this festive day.

00:57:18.650 --> 00:57:25.030
It is now my pleasure as director of the
Stanford MSX program, to present

00:57:25.030 --> 00:57:29.570
this year's graduates who will receive the
degree of master of science in management.

00:57:30.750 --> 00:57:35.520
The mission of the MSX program is to
provide experienced leaders, men and

00:57:35.520 --> 00:57:38.520
women who have already spent at least
eight years in professional and

00:57:38.520 --> 00:57:39.970
management roles.

00:57:39.970 --> 00:57:41.740
The opportunity to prepare themselves for

00:57:41.740 --> 00:57:45.200
increasingly senior positions in the
organizations they lead.

00:57:46.280 --> 00:57:51.130
The program is a full-time year-long
course of academic study.

00:57:51.130 --> 00:57:55.080
While studying at Stanford, these students
carry the title of Sloane Fellows.

00:57:56.350 --> 00:58:01.130
This year's 83 fellows came to Stanford
from across the United States and

00:58:01.130 --> 00:58:03.220
30 additional countries.

00:58:03.220 --> 00:58:06.400
Most fellows have families that join them
for the year.

00:58:06.400 --> 00:58:08.168
Many are sponsored by their employers.

00:58:08.168 --> 00:58:10.050
Others are self-sponsored and

00:58:10.050 --> 00:58:13.900
include those who will create innovative
new enterprises after graduation.

00:58:15.200 --> 00:58:18.550
Having completed all the academic
requirements of the program,

00:58:18.550 --> 00:58:22.410
this year's fellows will now join the
worldwide family of GSB alumni.

00:58:23.910 --> 00:58:26.620
On behalf of the administration of the
program, and

00:58:26.620 --> 00:58:29.250
the faculty who have taught them.

00:58:29.250 --> 00:58:32.306
Join me in wishing each of them great
fulfillment and

00:58:32.306 --> 00:58:34.880
success in the next phase of their
careers.

00:58:34.880 --> 00:58:43.033
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE].

