01:11:16.345 --> 01:11:21.128
Distinguished guests, faculty, staff,
family, and friends.

01:11:21.128 --> 01:11:24.888
The MBA students gathered before us today
achieve great distinction.

01:11:24.888 --> 01:11:26.353
[APPLAUSE] Two years ago,

01:11:26.353 --> 01:11:31.531
they successfully navigated our extremely
competitive admissions process, right.

01:11:31.531 --> 01:11:32.450
[APPLAUSE].
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

01:11:32.450 --> 01:11:35.735
&gt;&gt; Since then, there were quiet, solid
foundations in general management.

01:11:35.735 --> 01:11:39.004
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

01:11:39.004 --> 01:11:46.640
[APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; I love them.

01:11:46.640 --> 01:11:49.297
And have pursued deeper study in their
areas of interest.

01:11:49.297 --> 01:11:51.010
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

01:11:51.010 --> 01:11:53.390
&gt;&gt; They have engaged in personal growth
and

01:11:53.390 --> 01:11:56.430
built relationships that will last a
lifetime.

01:11:56.430 --> 01:12:01.290
They have helped the school and the
community in many extremely valuable ways.

01:12:01.290 --> 01:12:03.580
They are an impressive group and are ready
and

01:12:03.580 --> 01:12:07.210
worthy to join the ranks of our
illustrious alumni.

01:12:07.210 --> 01:12:10.202
Therefore ladies and gentlemen, it is my
great honor and

01:12:10.202 --> 01:12:13.582
privilege to present to you the Stanford
MBA Class of 2014.

01:12:13.582 --> 01:12:23.582
[APPLAUSE].

01:12:40.937 --> 01:12:45.393
You are the 89th MBA graduating class at
the Stanford GSB.

01:12:45.393 --> 01:12:47.308
And to echo what Phil Knight said,

01:12:47.308 --> 01:12:50.225
in my somewhat biased opinion, the best
class yet.

01:12:50.225 --> 01:12:55.333
&gt;&gt; [NOISE] [APPLAUSE].

01:12:55.333 --> 01:12:59.212
&gt;&gt; So as you leave to lead lives of impact
and meaning, I fully expect that your

01:12:59.212 --> 01:13:04.580
accomplishments at Stanford will pale in
comparison to your future achievements.

01:13:04.580 --> 01:13:07.530
But I hope your memories of the GSP will
remain fresh and

01:13:07.530 --> 01:13:10.610
that you'll continue to be involved with
the school.

01:13:10.610 --> 01:13:14.770
Our alumni played an important role in
your academic experience ranging from

01:13:14.770 --> 01:13:19.410
being judges during executive challenge to
coming back to be your lectures in

01:13:19.410 --> 01:13:21.180
entrepreneurial courses.

01:13:21.180 --> 01:13:25.260
It is my wish that you too will engage
with the GSP as alumni.

01:13:25.260 --> 01:13:29.280
And give your time and experience
generously to future classes.

01:13:29.280 --> 01:13:34.020
Your classes already demonstrated its
desires to stay connected to the GSB and

01:13:34.020 --> 01:13:37.360
to support the school in a meaningful way
through your participation in

01:13:37.360 --> 01:13:38.610
the class gift program.

01:13:39.810 --> 01:13:44.258
I must recognize the extraordinary result
of over 94% of you pledging to

01:13:44.258 --> 01:13:45.534
give back to the GSB.

01:13:45.534 --> 01:13:55.054
[APPLAUSE].

01:13:55.054 --> 01:13:57.860
We plan to make house calls to the other
6% very soon, okay?

01:13:59.480 --> 01:14:03.840
So you will leave your own legacy and play
a part in bringing the GSP experience to

01:14:03.840 --> 01:14:07.770
future generations, as other alumni have
done before you.

01:14:07.770 --> 01:14:12.145
At this time, I'd like to ask the Arbuckle
Leadership Fellows to stand.

01:14:12.145 --> 01:14:22.145
[APPLAUSE].

01:14:23.618 --> 01:14:26.177
The Arbuckle Leadership Fellows Program,
keep,

01:14:26.177 --> 01:14:29.746
keep standing, plays an integral role in
our leadership curriculum by

01:14:29.746 --> 01:14:32.958
bringing together a group of talented
second-year students to

01:14:32.958 --> 01:14:36.520
support the leadership development of the
MBA one class.

01:14:36.520 --> 01:14:39.305
On behalf of the GSB, I thank these 68
students for

01:14:39.305 --> 01:14:43.677
their tireless work, their extraordinary
dedication to their MBA one squads and

01:14:43.677 --> 01:14:46.655
coaches, and for inspiring an
unprecedented number of

01:14:46.655 --> 01:14:51.330
first-year students to seek out this
unique leadership opportunity.

01:14:51.330 --> 01:14:54.254
They are a role model for student
leadership at its best.

01:14:54.254 --> 01:14:56.048
Please join me in another round of
applause for

01:14:56.048 --> 01:14:57.480
this remarkable group of students.

01:14:57.480 --> 01:15:02.716
[APPLAUSE]

01:15:02.716 --> 01:15:09.262
[APPLAUSE].

01:15:09.262 --> 01:15:12.384
&gt;&gt; I'd now like to ask the student leaders
of the Global Study Trips,

01:15:12.384 --> 01:15:14.280
the Social Innovation Study Trips, and

01:15:14.280 --> 01:15:16.808
the Stanford-Tsinghua Exchange Program to
stand.

01:15:16.808 --> 01:15:18.526
[BLANK_AUDIO]

01:15:18.526 --> 01:15:24.581
[APPLAUSE] These 95, these 95 outstanding
student

01:15:24.581 --> 01:15:31.031
leaders partnered with the school on a
critical component

01:15:31.031 --> 01:15:38.460
of the GSB education, the Global
Experience Requirement.

01:15:38.460 --> 01:15:43.130
They've served as peer educators for over
600 students, traveling through 21

01:15:43.130 --> 01:15:47.030
countries, discovering how business fields
are relevant in a myriad industries and

01:15:47.030 --> 01:15:50.190
institutions, and proving what our faculty
teach them,

01:15:50.190 --> 01:15:52.115
which is the different countries are
different.

01:15:52.115 --> 01:15:52.870
[LAUGH] Okay?

01:15:54.040 --> 01:15:56.460
For their ambassadorship of the GSB, and

01:15:56.460 --> 01:15:59.350
their indelible impact on the students
they led, we thank them,

01:15:59.350 --> 01:16:03.475
please join me again, in a round of
applause for these students, okay?

01:16:03.475 --> 01:16:03.975
[APPLAUSE].
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

01:16:03.975 --> 01:16:11.950
I would also like

01:16:11.950 --> 01:16:14.110
to now acknowledge one of the faculty
sitting here.

01:16:15.260 --> 01:16:18.290
Any of you who took BS Financial
Accounting had Anne Beyer as

01:16:18.290 --> 01:16:19.075
your instructor.

01:16:19.075 --> 01:16:21.105
[APPLAUSE] 'Kay?

01:16:21.105 --> 01:16:22.880
[APPLAUSE].

01:16:22.880 --> 01:16:27.200
&gt;&gt; So as you now, Anne Beyer won the MBA
Distinguished Teaching Award last year.

01:16:27.200 --> 01:16:31.400
At commencement tomorrow, she is receiving
the Walter Gores Award for Excellence in

01:16:31.400 --> 01:16:34.645
teaching, which is the highest award for
teaching at Stanford University.

01:16:34.645 --> 01:16:38.405
[APPLAUSE]

01:16:38.405 --> 01:16:43.180
In the next few minutes we will begin
reading

01:16:44.420 --> 01:16:50.300
the names of the graduates in alphabetical
order, and will invite them forward to

01:16:50.300 --> 01:16:58.220
receive their diploma.

01:16:58.220 --> 01:17:01.202
Names will be read by Derrick Bolton,
Assistant Dean for

01:17:01.202 --> 01:17:03.608
the MBA Admissions, the person who brought
you here.

01:17:03.608 --> 01:17:08.838
[LAUGH] And Margaret, and Margaret Hayes,
Assistant Dean of the MBA Program,

01:17:08.838 --> 01:17:12.112
the person who's making sure you leave on
time.

01:17:12.112 --> 01:17:13.080
[LAUGH] 'Kay?

01:17:13.080 --> 01:17:16.890
Graduates will receive their diplomas from
Dean Garth Saloner.

01:17:16.890 --> 01:17:20.810
So all of you here have undoubtedly heard
of Arjay Miller, whom Phil alluded to, and

01:17:20.810 --> 01:17:22.120
Glen as well.

01:17:22.120 --> 01:17:25.270
It's my impression that many of the
graduating MBAs consider themselves

01:17:25.270 --> 01:17:26.256
friends of Arjay Miller.

01:17:26.256 --> 01:17:27.230
[LAUGH] 'Kay?

01:17:27.230 --> 01:17:30.161
[APPLAUSE]

01:17:30.161 --> 01:17:32.361
[LAUGH]

01:17:32.361 --> 01:17:37.860
So Arjay served in the US Air Force during
the Second World War, and was later one

01:17:37.860 --> 01:17:43.400
of the the so-called Whiz Kids who joined
Ford Motor Company and revolutionized it.

01:17:43.400 --> 01:17:46.080
And Arjay rose to become President of Ford
and

01:17:46.080 --> 01:17:51.184
then was the much admired fourth Dean of
the GSB from 1968 to 78.

01:17:51.184 --> 01:17:54.520
His sterling leadership of the school is
legendary, and

01:17:54.520 --> 01:17:59.480
in honor of Dean Arjay Miller's service,
the top 10% of the graduating class,

01:17:59.480 --> 01:18:03.840
ranked by academic performance, are
designated, Arjay Miller Scholars.

01:18:03.840 --> 01:18:05.950
So, as we read the names of the graduates,

01:18:05.950 --> 01:18:10.400
we will announce if they have achieved the
distinction of Arjay Miller Scholar.

01:18:10.400 --> 01:18:13.010
We will also acknowledge students in the
top 10% of the class,

01:18:13.010 --> 01:18:18.740
who are in Joint Degree Programs, and so,
will be graduating in subsequent years.

01:18:18.740 --> 01:18:20.516
So with that, Maggie and Derrick, could
you begin?

01:18:20.516 --> 01:18:29.014
